## Context

Found by the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09 (19:05-19:15 UTC, run
from the ~/CNRS session). `scripts/ticket-sweep.sh merged-probe` exits 2
(could-not-determine) on branches git or the forge can settle, so molt never
cleans them.

## Evidence

- (a) Default branch `master`: chemin-de-voix, every branch exits 2 with
  "git could not compare <branch> with main", including
  `codex/1463-check-fast`, a plain ancestor of origin/master.
- (b) Squash-landed branches whose ticket's `Closed:` line names no PR:
  padme `t0106-btrbk-cold`, search-works-for-zotero `t1141` and
  `ticket/0811`, chemin-de-voix `t1141`. `git cherry` and `git range-diff`
  show them landed.
- (c) Branches that map to no ticket by name: AEDIST's 78
  `tournament/<id>-*` branches; livre-milliards-climat has no `tickets/` at
  all, while the forge shows its PR #3 closed unmerged.

## Diagnosis

Established: exit 2 in all three classes, with the observations above. Not
established: whether (a) is a hard-coded `main` or a missing `origin/HEAD`
lookup; whether (c) should be settled by the probe or left to molt.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The probe detects the default branch (origin/HEAD, else main/master) instead of assuming `main`
- [ ] Patch-id evidence (`git cherry` all `-`, or equivalent) is accepted as a second landed signal
- [ ] Tests cover (a) and (b), with negative controls asserting exact exit codes

## Verify and Imagine (raid 4afdb3, 2026-11-09)
- Verified: (a) chemin-de-voix (master, origin/HEAD → origin/master): `merged-probe master~3`
  exits 2 "could not compare ... with main"; `main` hard-coded at scripts/ticket-sweep.sh:74, 76,
  86, 88 (four sites, settles the open question). (c) AEDIST's 78 tournament/* branches exit 2
  "does not map to a ticket"; livre-milliards-climat has no tickets/ so the top-level guard (:21-22)
  pre-empts any probe. (b) not reproducible: padme t0106-btrbk-cold and chemin-de-voix
  codex/1463-check-fast are gone since the sweep; closed ticket 0106 still has a Closed line
  without #N (landed as PR #251), so (b) lives on as a fixture only.
- Path: default_ref() = origin/HEAD, else local main/master (ladder as sync-local-main.sh:30-39;
  git_utils._default_branch, worktree-tmp-guard.py:65 and review_notes.py:306 have variants: inline
  copy, no shared helper); replace the four sites; `git cherry $base $branch` all `-` → exit 0, any
  `+` → fall through (a squash that dropped a file shows `+`, so it is safe). Tests in
  tests/test_ticket_sweep.py: master-default fixture with a bare origin and remote set-head;
  cherry-pick fixture with a Closed line without #N; negative controls with exact exit codes.
- Blind-Spot: molt never deletes on exit 1 or 2 (SKILL.md:243-250), so criterion 3 (forge
  closed-unmerged → exit 1) buys a log line and adds a forge dependency in adopter repos with
  different push identities (cired.digital); moving the tickets/ guard serves only that criterion.
  Stale branches are clutter: none of the three classes meets the severity floor.
- Author decisions: (1) drop criterion 3 and keep criteria 1, 2, 4; (2) ticket or inline fix.

## Author decisions (raid 5c2a37, 2026-11-09)
- Criterion 3 dropped (author, 2026-11-09): molt deletes on neither exit 1 nor exit 2, so a forge closed-unmerged lookup buys a log line for a forge dependency in adopter repos. Class (c) stays exit 2.
